# Commander Spock: "You may cast that card ... if that spell's mana value is equal to or less than the number of differently
# named lands you control." Bot1 has one differently named land, so the Grizzly Bears (mana value 2) on top of its own library
# is never offered; it is not a land either, so it is still the top card of the library and Bot1 draws it. Bot2's own Grizzly
# Bears is in Bot2's hand and stays there: the reveal is of "your library" only.

